    "description": "Mobilinx is the project company delivering the Hurontario LRT, now branded the Hazel McCallion Line, in Ontario. Its end users are public transit passengers in Mississauga and Brampton, while the direct counterparty is the public sector under a long-term DBFOM contract. The project is asset-heavy and concession-based, combining design, construction, financing, operations, and maintenance obligations. Public sources describe the line as an 18-kilometre system with 19 stops. John Laing's portfolio materials indicate a 35% equity interest in the project, while project-level revenue and the internal split within John Laing Investments Limited were not publicly disclosed. The master workbook associates the investment with John Laing Investments Limited, the vehicle backed by Equitix and KKR.",
